    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d910">

                <pb facs="0916" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2331</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-31T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 31, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3487. Consul at Liverpool has received private information to the effect that
                    German submarines have very recently sunk eight ships in St. George’s Channel
                    and that there are submarines off the Mersey bar as well. The steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Philadelphia</hi> has postponed her departure daily
                    since last Wednesday, and has now fixed upon Monday next probably, for the
                    United States. Other transatlantic liners are deferring sailing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
